#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# square_wave

#% text
# `square_wave(x)` gives the square wave of period 1: 1 when `x - floor(x) < 1/2`, -1 otherwise.

#% text
# `square_wave([a, b], x)` gives b on the first half of each period and a on the second.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# Lists are mapped element-wise; symbolic arguments stay unevaluated. The derivative is 0 away from the jumps.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
square_wave(0.2)
#% output
#= 1

#% cell
table(square_wave(x), [x, 0, 2, 2/3])
#% output
#= [1, -1, 1, 1]

#% cell
square_wave([0, 5], [0.4, 1.2, 3.6])
#% output
#= [5, 5, 0]

